{
  "id": "m03-power-mod-queries",
  "title": "Power Modulo m",
  "source": {
    "name": "Original exercise on binary exponentiation"
  },
  "rating": 1100,
  "tags": [
    "math",
    "binary-exponentiation",
    "modular-arithmetic"
  ],
  "statement": "For each of `t` triples `(a, b, m)`, print `a^b mod m`, where `a^0` is defined as `1` (so the answer is `1 mod m`, which is `0` when `m = 1`).\n\n**Input.** First line: `t`. Then `t` lines, each holding `a`, `b` and `m`.\n\n**Output.** `t` lines, one result per triple.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ t ≤ 300",
    "0 ≤ a, b ≤ 10^18",
    "1 ≤ m ≤ 10^9"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "b can be 10^18, so multiplying a by itself b times is impossible. Think about the binary representation of b.",
    "Square the base repeatedly (a, a^2, a^4, a^8, ...) and multiply into the result when the matching bit of b is 1.",
    "Reduce a modulo m first, start the result at 1 % m (not 1, because m may be 1), and reduce after every multiplication. With m up to 10^9 each product is below 10^18 and fits a signed 64-bit integer. In JavaScript use BigInt."
  ],
  "editorial": "Binary exponentiation: while `b > 0`, if the lowest bit of `b` is set multiply the result by the current base, then square the base and shift `b` right. That is about `log2(b) <= 60` iterations per query.\n\nDetails the tests check: `a` itself can be up to `10^18`, so reduce it first; `a^0 = 1` even for `a = 0`; and when `m = 1` every answer is `0`, so the result must start as `1 % m`. Because `m <= 10^9`, every intermediate product is below `10^18` and never overflows a signed 64-bit integer.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(log n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nt = int(data[0])\n# for each (a, b, m) print a^b mod m without calling pow(a, b, m)\n",
    "javascript": "// Use BigInt.\nconst t = Number(readLine());\n// each next line: a b m\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int t;\n    cin >> t;\n    // each query: a b m (long long)\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int t = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        // each query: a b m (long)\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nt = int(data[0])\nout = []\nfor i in range(t):\n    a = int(data[1 + 3 * i])\n    b = int(data[2 + 3 * i])\n    m = int(data[3 + 3 * i])\n    a %= m\n    r = 1 % m\n    while b:\n        if b & 1:\n            r = r * a % m\n        a = a * a % m\n        b >>= 1\n    out.append(str(r))\nprint('\\n'.join(out))\n",
    "javascript": "const tok = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) for (const t of line.split(/\\s+/)) if (t) tok.push(t);\nlet pos = 0;\nconst t = Number(tok[pos++]);\nconst out = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < t; i++) {\n  let a = BigInt(tok[pos++]);\n  let b = BigInt(tok[pos++]);\n  const m = BigInt(tok[pos++]);\n  a %= m;\n  let r = 1n % m;\n  while (b > 0n) {\n    if (b & 1n) r = (r * a) % m;\n    a = (a * a) % m;\n    b >>= 1n;\n  }\n  out.push(r.toString());\n}\nconsole.log(out.join('\\n'));\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int t;\n    cin >> t;\n    while (t--) {\n        long long a, b, m;\n        cin >> a >> b >> m;\n        a %= m;\n        long long r = 1 % m;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if (b & 1) r = r * a % m;\n            a = a * a % m;\n            b >>= 1;\n        }\n        cout << r << \"\\n\";\n    }\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int t = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        while (t-- > 0) {\n            long a = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n            long b = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n            long m = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n            a %= m;\n            long r = 1 % m;\n            while (b > 0) {\n                if ((b & 1) == 1) r = r * a % m;\n                a = a * a % m;\n                b >>= 1;\n            }\n            sb.append(r).append('\\n');\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"
  },
